## Optional KPA installation

Set `kpa.enabled=true` to install the Kedify Pod Autoscaler controller and CRD
with the Agent chart on Kubernetes 1.33–1.35. KPA installation is independent
from multicluster mode.

For dedicated multicluster reconciliation, enable KPA and the dedicated mode:

```yaml
global:
  features:
    multicluster:
      enabled: true
      type: dedicated
keda:
  enabled: true
kpa:
  enabled: true
```

Enable `global.features.kedifyPodAutoscalerEnabled=true` separately when the
Agent should collect KPA resource metrics and discover KPA metrics endpoints.
For an ordinary single-cluster bundled KEDA installation, enable KPA support
with `keda.kedify.kpa.enabled=true`.

Existing separate KPA installations can keep `kpa.enabled=false`.

The bundled KPA resolves the bundled KEDA endpoint in the Helm release
namespace. Override `kpa.keda.metricsAddress`, `kpa.keda.metricsAuthority`, or
`kpa.keda.certificateSecret` only when connecting KPA to a differently named
or separately installed KEDA operator. Inspect the remaining controller
settings with `helm show values oci://ghcr.io/kedify/charts/kpa`.

Dedicated mode enables KEDA/KPA remote reconciliation and selects KPA as
KEDA's default autoscaling class. The default distributed mode uses the
Agent's DistributedScaledObject/DistributedScaledJob controllers and does not
install KPA unless `kpa.enabled=true`. An explicitly enabled KPA remains in
single-cluster mode with the distributed workflow.

## Values

Prefer `global.features` when this chart installs KEDA/KPA so settings are
shared with the bundled controllers. `agent.features` configures only the
Agent; dedicated multicluster mode requires the global settings.

